# Universal Python Task Automation: Reference Architecture & Blueprint

> **Reference Version:** 1.0.0
> **Target Audience:** Autonomous AI Agents (Antigravity, Cursor, Muse), DevOps Engineers, Automation Bots
> **Compliance:** 100% Repository Coding Guidelines, Monadic Error Handling, Zero Magic Strings, Universal LF

---

## 1. Architectural Overview & Mental Model

This directory provides the canonical reference architecture for autonomous, cross-platform Python task automation. Whenever an AI or engineer is tasked with building an automated task—such as Windows audio troubleshooting, VMware network resets, application cache cleanup, OS disk space optimization, or account provisioning—this directory serves as the executable blueprint.

### Core Architectural Pillars

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Cross-Platform Launchers                 │
│                 run.ps1 (Win)  │  run.sh (POSIX)            │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘
                               │ Discovers Python & Forwards
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  scripts/cli_dispatcher.py                  │
│       • Argparse CLI   • Interactive Suggestions Engine      │
│       • Top-Level Error Unwrapping & ExitCodeType Exit       │
└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬───────────────┘
               │                              │
               ▼                              ▼
┌──────────────────────────────┐ ┌────────────────────────────┐
│      scripts/task_runner.py  │ │   scripts/task_logger.py   │
│ • Modular Handlers (<= 15 L) │ │ • Console ANSI Badges      │
│ • Monadic Result[T] Returns  │ │ • Structured logs/task.log │
│ • Leaf Error Sovereignty     │ │ • JSON Audit Telemetry     │
└──────────────┬───────────────┘ └────────────────────────────┘
               │
               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              scripts/core_enums.py & core_constants.py      │
│     • Strongly-typed enums ending in Type with parse()      │
│     • Immutable constants classes (Zero Magic Strings)      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

1. **Leaf Error Sovereignty:** Leaf functions in `scripts/task_runner.py` return `Result[T]`. They NEVER call `sys.exit()` or unhandled raises.
2. **Outer Caller Exit:** Only `scripts/cli_dispatcher.py` unwraps `Result[T]` to terminate the process with strongly-typed `ExitCodeType`.
3. **Zero Magic Strings:** All strings (actions, categories, exit codes, badges, paths, packages) derive from enums ending in `Type` or constant classes.
4. **Strict Hygiene Invariants:** Every function $\le 15$ lines, every file $\le 200$ lines, positive booleans (`is_*`, `has_*`), zero nested `if` statements, 100% UNIX LF (`\n`, 0 CRLF).

